WEBVTT

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:02.050
Come on.

00:00:36.620 --> 00:01:00.000
The End

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:29.280
His eyes were burning with flames of hate, and his guns were loaded with poison bait, as they hauled, and swung, and outlawed, fell away, and outlawed, and slied.

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:39.940
So hot on the tail of the outlaw's trail, this cowboy road ready to dive.

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:44.750
Grease up your guns, outlaw, and pinch them on tight.

00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:49.010
There'll be blood a-running in town before night.

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:53.120
There'll be guns a-blazin' and singin' with lead.

00:01:53.120 --> 00:02:00.000
Tonight you'll be drinkin' your drinks with.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:02.310
the dead.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:38.550
A shot in the back, huh?

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:40.920
Don't try to talk, Sheriff.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:09.040
A nasty wound.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:12.620
Stop bleeding, though, that's something.

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:14.990
You're going to be all right.

00:03:14.990 --> 00:03:20.120
I'll have you in Starbucks before night.

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:22.340
Just to swallow now.

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:23.520
You can have more.

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:13.410
We got it!

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:59.800
- Are you hurt, miss? - I don't think so.

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:04.000
- Are they coming? - They're almost here.

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:07.120
They mustn't take me. Really, they mustn't.

00:05:07.290 --> 00:05:09.950
Please don't let them. I'm not a bandit.

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:13.090
Really, I'm not. You see?

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:19.870
Hey, hey, this is the best place here, Elmer. Give me a push.

00:05:22.390 --> 00:05:25.700
- Hi, you know, I'm next. - Don't you understand?

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:28.900
It was our only way out. Won't you please help me?

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:40.690
I'll do what I can for you miss your horse is done for well, you'll have to take mine

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:59.000
I'll have your horse in town for you in an hour

00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:26.240
You got his horse, Bert.

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:28.590
Yeah, it's too bad I didn't get the road agent.

00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:30.000
Well, he can't get far.

00:06:38.990 --> 00:06:39.670
We got it!

00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:49.170
We lost him. You go that way.

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:22.980
Come on, Bert, this ain't getting us nowhere.

00:08:44.840 --> 00:08:46.160
- You got what?

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:48.110
Where in the world have you been?

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:49.750
- I beat the robber to it.

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:52.250
I held up the stage and I got our money.

00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:53.850
- You held up the stage?

00:08:53.850 --> 00:08:55.590
Why never-- - I don't get excited.

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:59.700
It's all over and I'm safe, but I lost proof.

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:01.560
They shot him from under me.

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:04.340
And if it hadn't been for a stranger lending me his horse,

00:09:04.340 --> 00:09:05.870
I guess I'd be in jail by now.

00:09:05.870 --> 00:09:08.150
A stranger? Well, who was he?

00:09:08.150 --> 00:09:11.060
I don't know, but he sure was swell.

00:09:11.060 --> 00:09:13.640
I've got to change my clothes and get his horse back into town.

00:09:13.640 --> 00:09:16.840
I've never heard of anything like that before in all my life.

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:38.430
- The boys are sure late.

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:41.010
I wonder if anything's happened.

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:58.200
- There she comes now.

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:00.000
- Down there, my irons.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:06.670
Well hand down the bag you're late now. There ain't no bag a mask rider held us up about two miles back

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:14.790
What'll the boss say we can't help what he says it ain't our fault. Well, we'll see you in town

00:10:14.790 --> 00:10:17.730
Oh

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:03.920
Well, Pete, we got stuck up again.

00:11:04.140 --> 00:11:04.920
Where did it happen?

00:11:05.020 --> 00:11:06.240
Down by Big Rock Canyon.

00:11:06.510 --> 00:11:07.760
What kind of a horse was he riding?

00:11:07.940 --> 00:11:08.380
A bay.

00:11:09.150 --> 00:11:11.630
We shot the horse, but the rider got away.

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:14.460
We might trace the brand and find the owner.

00:11:14.780 --> 00:11:16.480
By George, we never thought to look at the brand.

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:18.740
We'll ride up there and see what we can find.

00:11:20.800 --> 00:11:23.540
How do you do, Miss Denton?

00:11:23.990 --> 00:11:24.810
How's your father?

00:11:25.150 --> 00:11:25.930
Better, thank you.

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:28.430
Oh, Pete, was there a package for me today?

00:11:28.590 --> 00:11:30.000
There was, but the stage was hanging.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:36.620
held up. Again? Where's the sheriff? He hasn't got back yet. You know, he went out to try and break up

00:11:36.620 --> 00:11:42.820
this road agent gang. We haven't been able to find him. Can I be of any assistance? Well, my horse and

00:11:42.820 --> 00:11:48.010
saddle was stolen last night. I thought maybe he might be able to help me find them. What color was

00:11:48.010 --> 00:11:53.480
your horse? He was a sort of a bay with a double O brand. Well, there was a horse of that description

00:11:53.480 --> 00:12:00.000
just shot. Oh, I hope it wasn't mine. If it was, Miss Denton, I'll bring your saddle.

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:12.570
Howdy, folks. Could you tell me where the sheriff is?

00:12:12.570 --> 00:12:17.180
Well, I take charge when he isn't here. Can I do anything for you?

00:12:17.180 --> 00:12:19.930
Thanks. I'll wait for him.

00:12:19.930 --> 00:12:24.570
The sheriff didn't care especially for this job. He might not come back.

00:12:24.570 --> 00:12:29.460
I'll take that chance. I have an idea he will come back.

00:12:40.680 --> 00:12:43.930
I don't like the way that fellow talks.

00:12:43.930 --> 00:12:55.680
We'll watch him.

00:12:55.680 --> 00:12:58.070
Meet me at the crossroads, and I'll take you home.

00:13:13.340 --> 00:13:15.300
- That mass damage story was on the square, huh?

00:13:15.300 --> 00:13:17.860
- Yeah, he got us two miles ahead of the boys here.

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:19.260
- Well, he's a foot now.

00:13:19.260 --> 00:13:21.680
The only place he can get water is the Dentons or town.

00:13:21.680 --> 00:13:23.310
We may get him.

00:13:23.310 --> 00:13:25.220
Let's have a look at that horse.

00:13:56.620 --> 00:13:57.810
It's a good idea.

00:13:57.810 --> 00:14:00.000
I reckon he's pretty enough.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:13.220
You were right. She is thirsty.

00:14:13.220 --> 00:14:16.220
Come on. I want you to meet my dad.

00:14:16.220 --> 00:14:18.220
Why, sure, I'd be glad to.

00:14:18.220 --> 00:14:26.920
Dad, I want you to meet Mr. Saunders.

00:14:26.920 --> 00:14:30.000
I want to thank you, young fellow.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:36.060
for what you've done for my daughter forget it but what's happened to you sit down I'll tell you

00:14:36.060 --> 00:14:45.350
all about it thank you you see Fay and me own half interest in the mine at Yucca our partner sends

00:14:45.350 --> 00:14:51.600
us our share every couple of weeks sometimes it's only a few dollars other times it's a few hundred

00:14:51.600 --> 00:14:57.420
he always writes as when to expect it and almost always the stage was held up when a shipment came

00:14:57.420 --> 00:15:00.000
through one day we discovered

00:15:00.220 --> 00:15:01.710
- Our letters were being opened.

00:15:01.710 --> 00:15:04.140
- They knew just when the money was coming,

00:15:04.140 --> 00:15:06.600
so I decided to follow the stage.

00:15:06.600 --> 00:15:12.890
See, I ran into the holdup and got a slug in me hip.

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:16.370
Today, Fay thought she'd beat 'em to it.

00:15:16.370 --> 00:15:17.590
That's when you happened into it.

00:15:30.570 --> 00:15:32.280
- It's Kincaid with my saddle.

00:15:32.280 --> 00:15:34.640
Wait here, I'll get him on his way.

00:15:34.640 --> 00:15:43.250
- It was your horse all right, Miss Denton.

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:44.740
Here's your saddle.

00:15:44.740 --> 00:15:45.920
- Thank you so much.

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:46.870
- Not at all.

00:15:46.870 --> 00:15:49.230
Bert, take it out to the barn.

00:15:49.230 --> 00:15:50.930
- Never mind, don't trouble.

00:15:50.930 --> 00:15:56.290
- When your father's feeling better,

00:15:56.290 --> 00:15:58.800
I'd like to talk to him about buying your ranch.

00:15:58.800 --> 00:16:00.000
- He's too ill to talk about.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:23.230
- Now.

00:16:23.230 --> 00:16:25.510
- Give him my regard.

00:16:25.510 --> 00:16:26.470
- Thank you, I will.

00:16:39.340 --> 00:16:48.380
Hey, Chief, you know that Umbre what was looking for the sheriff?

00:16:48.380 --> 00:16:49.470
Yes.

00:16:49.470 --> 00:16:53.260
Well, his horse is in Denton's barn.

00:16:53.260 --> 00:16:56.060
I wonder what his game is.

00:16:56.060 --> 00:17:00.000
Well, whatever it is, we'll put a stop to it right here.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:01.000
He's got to come along this road.

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:02.000
Accidents will happen.

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:03.850
I get you.

00:17:03.850 --> 00:17:04.850
What about the sheriff?

00:17:04.850 --> 00:17:05.850
Can he do something?

00:17:05.850 --> 00:17:16.200
It's mighty strange, but Bill Baxter's gone.

00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:19.190
He's the second sheriff to disappear in a year.

00:17:19.190 --> 00:17:23.100
He was a fine man and our friend.

00:17:23.100 --> 00:17:26.270
Why is Kincaid so anxious?

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:29.660
Why is Kincaid so anxious?

00:17:29.660 --> 00:17:30.000
I don't know.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:31.410
is to buy your ranch.

00:17:31.410 --> 00:17:34.270
He's trying to buy up all the ranches.

00:17:34.270 --> 00:17:37.230
And he's offering the boys the ridiculous price

00:17:37.230 --> 00:17:39.150
of a dollar an acre.

00:17:39.150 --> 00:17:42.340
He owns the water rights to Lost Creek.

00:17:42.340 --> 00:17:47.630
You see, Lost Creek comes up and disappears on his land.

00:17:47.630 --> 00:17:50.750
He supplies the whole country hereabouts with water.

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:52.510
That's why he's so independent.

00:17:52.510 --> 00:17:55.460
No one will fight him for fear he'll shut off their supply.

00:17:55.460 --> 00:17:58.070
I'm the only one who can talk back to him.

00:17:58.070 --> 00:18:00.000
I've got the only well in Antelope Valley.

00:18:01.340 --> 00:18:05.910
- The boys are holding a meeting in town today.

00:18:05.910 --> 00:18:09.770
- Say you men, we're getting a rotten deal.

00:18:09.770 --> 00:18:13.600
Forced to sell our land for nothing or no water.

00:18:13.600 --> 00:18:15.350
- I'll fight first.

00:18:15.350 --> 00:18:17.330
- But he's got real gunmen.

00:18:17.330 --> 00:18:19.240
What about our families?

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:21.570
- Oh, you can't start a fight now.

00:18:21.570 --> 00:18:24.250
Give Washington a chance to answer our letter.

00:18:24.250 --> 00:18:25.810
They're bound to send somebody out here

00:18:25.810 --> 00:18:27.650
to investigate Baxter's disappearance.

00:18:27.650 --> 00:18:28.710
- That's right.

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:29.540
- Well,

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:34.380
We must wait until we see what he says when he learns we've decided not to sell.

00:18:34.380 --> 00:18:38.460
Well, I hope you'll be feeling better, Mr. Denton.

00:18:38.460 --> 00:18:39.380
Thank you.

00:18:39.380 --> 00:18:42.160
And I may accept that invitation of yours to stay here.

00:18:42.160 --> 00:18:43.280
We'd love to have you.

00:18:43.280 --> 00:18:44.280
We sure would, son.

00:18:44.280 --> 00:18:48.920
Well, thank you.

00:18:48.920 --> 00:18:57.270
Good-bye.

00:18:57.270 --> 00:19:00.000
They may have seen your horse at the barn.

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:01.000
I'll be back for dinner.

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:14.650
Well, gentlemen, have you reached an agreement?

00:19:14.650 --> 00:19:15.540
Yes.

00:19:15.540 --> 00:19:17.750
We've decided you can go plumb to--

00:19:17.750 --> 00:19:18.750
Wait, Mason.

00:19:18.750 --> 00:19:20.750
Your proposition, Kincaid, is beyond all reason.

00:19:20.750 --> 00:19:23.920
We've worked years for these lands,

00:19:23.920 --> 00:19:25.970
and we don't intend to settle for a few million dollars.

00:19:25.970 --> 00:19:26.970
That's your opinion.

00:19:26.970 --> 00:19:27.860
I'm not sure.

00:19:27.860 --> 00:19:28.870
I'm not sure.

00:19:28.870 --> 00:19:30.000
I'm not sure.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:33.920
privilege don't forget the state has needed me the right to the only water in this valley

00:19:33.920 --> 00:19:39.040
i've spent hard-earned money for labor and dams and i expect to get it back you're getting it

00:19:39.040 --> 00:19:44.690
back ain't you we're paying you a big price for your water now in three days my contract to furnish

00:19:44.690 --> 00:19:49.170
you with water expires you will either sell at my price or pay four times the amount for water

00:19:49.170 --> 00:19:53.200
you're paying now so settle it among yourselves

00:20:23.520 --> 00:20:24.420
Here he comes now.

00:20:34.410 --> 00:20:35.800
Come on, get together.

00:21:02.970 --> 00:21:05.970
Now you boys are going for a nice little ride.

00:21:05.970 --> 00:21:28.900
What have you got here? Sit down.

00:21:32.460 --> 00:21:35.010
- What's the trouble? - Nothing right now.

00:21:35.190 --> 00:21:41.380
But anything might happen. I need protection.

00:21:41.730 --> 00:21:46.090
- What's it worth? - Same as before.

00:21:49.710 --> 00:21:54.000
There'll be blood a-running in town before night.

00:21:54.410 --> 00:21:58.640
There'll be guns a-blazin' and singin' with Liz.

00:21:58.790 --> 00:22:00.000
Tonight you'll be drunk.

00:22:00.120 --> 00:22:05.130
Your drinks with the dead.

00:22:05.130 --> 00:22:12.160
- Who's that? - I don't know.

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.950
Huh, what a fine pair of lovebirds you turned out to be.

00:22:55.630 --> 00:22:56.330
Howdy, man.

00:22:56.690 --> 00:22:59.070
All right, I'm looking for a Mr. Taylor.

00:22:59.310 --> 00:22:59.910
I'm Taylor.

00:23:01.440 --> 00:23:04.220
Found this letter a few miles back on the road.

00:23:04.220 --> 00:23:12.800
Must have been dropped in that last stagecoach holdup.

00:23:12.800 --> 00:23:14.860
Boys, here's our answer from Washington.

00:23:14.860 --> 00:23:16.850
Good, good!

00:23:16.850 --> 00:23:20.270
Dear Mr. Taylor, in answer to your letter of May the 10th,

00:23:20.270 --> 00:23:22.330
please be advised that we are sending a man

00:23:22.330 --> 00:23:24.430
to investigate the situation you mentioned

00:23:24.430 --> 00:23:25.770
as soon as possible.

00:23:25.770 --> 00:23:26.980
All right?

00:23:30.030 --> 00:23:32.070
- There, I hope he gets here soon.

00:23:32.070 --> 00:23:34.610
- Now we'll show Mr. King, can't you?

00:23:34.610 --> 00:23:36.560
- Yeah, what an all.

00:24:06.880 --> 00:24:08.780
Oh, glad to see you out, Mr. Denton.

00:24:08.920 --> 00:24:10.710
Yep, getting better every day.

00:24:12.350 --> 00:24:14.390
Say, uh, is that the old creek bed?

00:24:14.670 --> 00:24:15.050
Yeah.

00:24:15.680 --> 00:24:19.600
When I first come here, it was running water through every ranch in the valley.

00:24:20.040 --> 00:24:21.300
Then it dried up.

00:24:22.840 --> 00:24:24.820
That's when Kincaid got the upper hand.

00:24:26.800 --> 00:24:28.510
You can't divert a stream, can you?

00:24:28.570 --> 00:24:30.000
No, that's again the law.

00:24:31.440 --> 00:24:34.040
Well, those water contracts expire today at noon.

00:24:34.900 --> 00:24:36.900
I think I'll take a run in town and see what happens.

00:24:37.000 --> 00:24:38.100
Yeah, that's a good idea.

00:24:40.360 --> 00:24:41.780
I'll be glad to hear about it.

00:25:00.160 --> 00:25:04.080
Here comes Kincaid now.

00:25:08.410 --> 00:25:11.690
Well, gentlemen, it's noon.

00:25:12.260 --> 00:25:13.920
My contract with you has expired.

00:25:14.430 --> 00:25:15.490
Have you come to any decision?

00:25:15.870 --> 00:25:18.310
Kincaid, you've got the soul of a snake.

00:25:18.430 --> 00:25:19.250
We won't go into that.

00:25:19.530 --> 00:25:20.670
This is a business proposition.

00:25:21.050 --> 00:25:22.690
The law is on my side.

00:25:23.300 --> 00:25:25.020
Now, what have you decided to do?

00:25:25.160 --> 00:25:25.960
Just this.

00:25:26.320 --> 00:25:30.000
We're hanging on to our land, and we are not paying you your price.

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:30.680
for your water.

00:25:30.940 --> 00:25:31.880
All right.

00:25:32.840 --> 00:25:34.500
Then take the consequences.

00:25:35.080 --> 00:25:36.380
Boys, turn off the water.

00:25:36.810 --> 00:25:38.610
Guard my dam, and if anyone

00:25:38.610 --> 00:25:40.790
sets foot on my land, shoot.

00:25:48.660 --> 00:25:50.460
Well, Kincaid may get more

00:25:50.460 --> 00:25:51.860
shooting than he's looking for.

00:25:53.980 --> 00:25:54.960
Just a minute, man.

00:25:54.960 --> 00:25:56.700
All right? Just a minute.

00:25:58.000 --> 00:26:00.000
I'm sure Denton will give you all the water you

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:05.450
Well, we may call on him for drinking water, but he can't supply enough for our stock and crops.

00:26:05.450 --> 00:26:09.450
If that man from Washington would only come, we'd have to buy somebody.

00:26:13.450 --> 00:26:15.580
That sure was a good dinner.

00:26:15.580 --> 00:26:17.640
So glad you enjoyed it.

00:26:17.640 --> 00:26:20.030
Where do you taste them hot biscuits in the morning?

00:26:20.030 --> 00:26:22.270
Oh, pity.

00:26:22.270 --> 00:26:24.930
Dad's crazy about hot biscuits.

00:26:24.930 --> 00:26:26.830
Well, who wouldn't be?

00:26:26.830 --> 00:26:28.450
Hehehehe.

00:26:30.440 --> 00:26:33.970
Gee, that was beautiful. Won't you sing the chorus again?

00:26:33.970 --> 00:26:36.440
That was mighty fine, son.

00:27:04.600 --> 00:27:05.410
Come on.

00:28:02.110 --> 00:28:14.190
I could listen to that all night.

00:28:15.230 --> 00:28:17.440
I enjoyed that so much.

00:28:18.240 --> 00:28:19.750
Please sing another one.

00:28:58.700 --> 00:28:59.830
Remember what I told you.

00:29:00.540 --> 00:29:05.380
- If anyone tries to get water, shoot. - All right, boss.

00:29:11.830 --> 00:29:14.440
- All fixed up? - Yes, he's full of the brim.

00:29:15.650 --> 00:29:18.330
- Mason, in case of trouble, keep on going. - All right.

00:29:18.330 --> 00:29:21.060
- I'll be right behind you. - Keep your eyes open.

00:29:21.220 --> 00:29:24.320
- You'll have a good trouble. - Oh, don't worry. We'll get to it.

00:29:24.730 --> 00:29:26.890
- We'll see you at dinner. - Bye.

00:29:27.170 --> 00:29:28.520
- Hold on, son.

00:29:35.950 --> 00:29:39.710
Dad, what are we going to do about Kincaid's office?

00:29:42.330 --> 00:29:46.910
Well, Faye, I've decided we'd better stick with the boys and their families.

00:29:47.650 --> 00:29:48.330
You're right.

00:29:48.800 --> 00:29:51.670
You ride down and tell Kincaid that we ain't selling.

00:29:52.440 --> 00:29:53.460
I sure will.

00:29:58.670 --> 00:29:59.880
I got more water from tenants.

00:30:00.060 --> 00:30:01.060
I expected that.

00:30:01.520 --> 00:30:03.720
I've got my men posted and they'll never get through.

00:30:04.240 --> 00:30:07.450
Besides, I've made Denton an offer he can't refuse.

00:30:10.350 --> 00:30:12.530
I'll own his place before night.

00:30:16.120 --> 00:30:21.860
Here he comes.

00:32:12.060 --> 00:32:12.710
Don't take it to me.

00:32:33.770 --> 00:32:46.130
We're going to get him down.

00:33:18.560 --> 00:33:22.800
- First drove the wagon. - Yes, huh?

00:33:22.800 --> 00:33:27.620
I give you the signal. You come down the middle of the street.

00:33:27.620 --> 00:33:29.660
I'm ordering this saunders out of town.

00:33:30.120 --> 00:33:33.180
And he may be just fool enough to fight it out with you.

00:33:34.360 --> 00:33:36.100
I'll be ready for him.

00:33:44.010 --> 00:33:46.310
I tell you, men, this has got to stop.

00:33:47.110 --> 00:33:48.070
Your cattle's dying.

00:33:48.870 --> 00:33:49.950
Your crops are withering.

00:33:50.740 --> 00:33:52.660
You're fighting a hopeless fight.

00:33:53.460 --> 00:33:55.360
Kincaid's got the law behind him.

00:33:56.070 --> 00:33:57.750
Sign up and take your licking.

00:33:58.650 --> 00:34:00.000
Sign up and stop.

00:34:00.670 --> 00:34:01.870
Bloodshed.

00:34:10.570 --> 00:34:14.350
Saunders, you've been afeared in my business once too often.

00:34:14.490 --> 00:34:19.040
Now I'm giving you just one minute to get out of town.

00:34:58.990 --> 00:34:59.760
- Miss Hedden?

00:35:04.860 --> 00:35:09.050
- There's gonna be a shootin'!

00:35:21.640 --> 00:35:23.640
- Why, that's Singin' Sandy.

00:35:23.640 --> 00:35:25.350
- Who?

00:35:25.350 --> 00:35:30.000
- The most notorious gunman since Billy the Kid.

00:35:38.160 --> 00:35:41.400
Go fast, Lippery. This is your last draw.

00:35:51.240 --> 00:35:53.140
You'll never handle guns again, Morgan.

00:36:03.480 --> 00:36:04.580
Right through the wrist.

00:36:04.640 --> 00:36:06.240
You better get him over to the doctor.

00:36:10.880 --> 00:36:13.410
Sunders, I guess you win.

00:36:14.110 --> 00:36:17.440
- Can I talk to you a minute? - Sure, I'll talk to you.

00:36:20.670 --> 00:36:23.270
- Hey, you? - He's singing Sandy, I tell you.

00:36:24.350 --> 00:36:26.500
I saw him do the same thing down on the border.

00:36:27.340 --> 00:36:29.560
Is he a killer?

00:36:30.090 --> 00:36:32.210
She's got a reputation from here to Kentucky.

00:36:36.310 --> 00:36:47.620
I need you, and I'll pay your price.

00:36:48.460 --> 00:36:49.200
What's the job?

00:36:49.440 --> 00:36:51.140
Protecting me and my interests.

00:36:51.650 --> 00:36:53.030
The law's on my side.

00:36:53.470 --> 00:36:56.110
But the sheriff's gone, and these ranchers may start trouble.

00:36:57.480 --> 00:36:59.060
I need a gunman.

00:37:02.300 --> 00:37:05.320
Are they enough? I'll take the job.

00:37:06.170 --> 00:37:07.720
Now, how about these Dentons?

00:37:07.970 --> 00:37:10.500
I've made them an offer they can't refuse.

00:37:10.660 --> 00:37:12.100
Oh, why pay them anything?

00:37:12.760 --> 00:37:15.750
Just drop a charge of dynamite down their well and collapse it.

00:37:16.650 --> 00:37:19.110
They'll have no water and then, like the rest of the ranchers,

00:37:19.250 --> 00:37:20.800
they'll have to sell out for nothing.

00:37:21.240 --> 00:37:24.680
That's an idea. Send in the boys.

00:37:41.770 --> 00:37:56.640
Kincaid wants you to talk to your ranchers confidentially.

00:37:56.720 --> 00:37:59.060
- Why, certainly, Mr. Saunders. - Why, of course.

00:38:05.980 --> 00:38:09.080
Now listen, boys, Saunders is working with us now.

00:38:09.530 --> 00:38:11.650
So let bygones be bygones.

00:38:13.400 --> 00:38:15.240
We're going to blow up Denton's well.

00:38:15.870 --> 00:38:19.350
And I want you to get enough dynamite to collapse it for good.

00:38:20.800 --> 00:38:24.690
If what you say is true, Saunders, we'll owe you a lot.

00:38:25.790 --> 00:38:28.590
Well, it's a long chance, but I say take it.

00:38:29.470 --> 00:38:30.000
Well...

00:38:30.030 --> 00:38:34.800
We were going to sign the contract anyway, so we'll insist on that clause.

00:38:34.800 --> 00:38:36.980
Good.

00:38:40.980 --> 00:38:44.500
You boys ready? I'll go along and watch old Denton.

00:38:44.500 --> 00:38:46.540
Now it'll take a big charge...

00:38:46.540 --> 00:38:48.540
I'll get enough to blow it to China.

00:38:48.540 --> 00:38:49.560
Good.

00:39:07.230 --> 00:39:14.570
We are ready to sign, Kincaid, providing you are willing to insert a new clause in our contract.

00:39:14.870 --> 00:39:15.560
What is it?

00:39:15.560 --> 00:39:30.000
That if you should fail at any time during the life of our contract to provide us with water, your water rights and lands become community programs.

00:39:31.150 --> 00:39:33.790
- Sure, I'll agree to that.

00:39:33.790 --> 00:40:00.000
Come on in.

00:40:01.340 --> 00:40:03.460
He's a gunman and a killer.

00:40:03.460 --> 00:40:05.540
Throw and shoot a man in town.

00:40:05.540 --> 00:40:07.490
And then he joined Kincaid's gang.

00:40:07.490 --> 00:40:09.950
Why, I can't believe it.

00:40:09.950 --> 00:40:12.420
I heard him tell Kincaid not to pay us in.

00:40:12.420 --> 00:40:13.580
And he's planning to blow up our well

00:40:13.580 --> 00:40:15.780
so we won't have any water.

00:40:15.780 --> 00:40:17.990
Oh, blow up our well, eh?

00:40:17.990 --> 00:40:21.210
We'll see about that.

00:40:21.210 --> 00:40:22.440
Let's have a look in his room.

00:40:43.600 --> 00:40:47.980
Well, that's Bill Baxter's stock.

00:40:47.980 --> 00:40:51.310
Maybe he killed the sheriff.

00:40:51.310 --> 00:41:00.000
And when I get inside you,

00:41:00.000 --> 00:41:03.680
- Let's do this job right. - Leave it to us.

00:41:03.800 --> 00:41:16.230
- Him now. - Don't let out.

00:41:16.350 --> 00:41:28.020
- Hello, Dad. I just saw Kincaid. - I know you did.

00:41:28.140 --> 00:41:30.000
I heard everything about him.

00:41:31.080 --> 00:41:32.810
- Well, that must have been interesting.

00:41:32.810 --> 00:41:34.510
- We know who you are, Mr. Singing Sandy.

00:41:34.510 --> 00:41:37.250
- You may be a killer and do away with sheriffs,

00:41:37.250 --> 00:41:39.430
but you ain't never gonna blow up my well.

00:42:50.600 --> 00:42:52.560
That's one job we did, right?

00:42:52.640 --> 00:42:55.120
Yeah, we opened up the whole Pacific Ocean.

00:43:04.320 --> 00:43:07.100
We better clear out of here before Kincaid catches up with us.

00:43:11.760 --> 00:43:18.260
Tomorrow, Kincaid's dam will be nothing but a mud hole.

00:43:19.890 --> 00:43:21.990
Your well was the headwaters of Lost Creek.

00:43:22.390 --> 00:43:24.710
Yeah, but Bill Baxter's badge.

00:43:24.810 --> 00:43:27.150
Oh, he made a deputy of me not knowing who I was.

00:43:29.090 --> 00:43:30.000
He'll be here today.

00:43:30.440 --> 00:43:35.600
- Who are you? - Sandy, but I was here by Washington.

00:43:43.600 --> 00:43:46.260
You can ride, Dad. Let's get in on a farm.

00:44:00.280 --> 00:44:23.810
- Well, then, now that the contracts are all signed and witnessed, I'll have the boys

00:44:23.810 --> 00:44:27.080
turn on the water.

00:45:30.190 --> 00:45:31.410
What a sign!

00:46:00.570 --> 00:46:01.160
Ha, ha, ha.

00:46:36.110 --> 00:46:41.300
- Hi Charlie! - I'm glad to see you, Sheriff!

00:47:02.430 --> 00:47:20.060
Hey, man, go and blow Denton's well and turn the moose the whole river.

00:47:20.060 --> 00:47:29.670
He'll rock himself what he don't want, he'll all be dry, and we'll all...

00:47:34.000 --> 00:47:43.610
Wrong, Kincaid.

00:47:43.610 --> 00:47:47.960
I've been tricked, ruined, and now I'm getting even.

00:48:00.990 --> 00:48:14.310
You tried to finish me, but young Saunders here saved my life.

00:48:15.330 --> 00:48:24.320
Sheriff, it's you bastard.

00:48:24.340 --> 00:48:30.000
I'll tell you boys, I started out.

00:48:30.030 --> 00:48:32.950
He was down across the desert, heading for Starla.

00:48:32.950 --> 00:48:36.390
He didn't fade and one of his young men followed me.

00:48:36.390 --> 00:48:44.760
When they got the chance, they slugged me in the back.

00:48:44.760 --> 00:48:54.440
You finished him, double-crosser?

00:49:04.250 --> 00:49:04.870
I can't.

00:49:30.760 --> 00:49:38.710
- I killed Warren, and I shot you, Kincaid.

00:49:41.140 --> 00:49:48.340
- Hey, who is he?

00:49:48.340 --> 00:49:49.760
- I thought you all knew who he was.

00:49:49.760 --> 00:49:51.290
- No!

00:49:51.290 --> 00:49:53.140
- He's in the secret service.

00:49:53.140 --> 00:49:54.800
- He's your man from Washington.

00:49:54.800 --> 00:49:55.800
- No!

00:49:55.800 --> 00:49:56.850
- Yeah!

00:49:56.850 --> 00:50:00.000
- No, no, no, no!

00:51:04.280 --> 00:51:07.710
- Well, I suppose you're leaving us. - Yep.

00:51:07.790 --> 00:51:09.880
I'm going to Yucca to send a wire.

00:51:09.960 --> 00:51:11.730
Oh.

00:51:12.320 --> 00:51:14.900
Son, we all make mistakes.

00:51:14.980 --> 00:51:19.620
And I know somebody that's taking her mighty serious.

00:51:19.700 --> 00:51:26.960
You suppose you could go in and tell her you like her biscuits or something to cheer her up a bit?

00:51:27.140 --> 00:51:28.900
I'm going to tell her more than that, Dad.

00:51:51.310 --> 00:51:53.620
You're going away, aren't you?

00:51:53.620 --> 00:51:55.160
Yes.

00:51:55.160 --> 00:51:59.410
I don't want you to.

00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:01.460
But I'll be back for supper.

00:52:01.460 --> 00:52:03.840
That is, if you'll bake me about a hundred biscuits.
